I look in the large mirror in the shop.
This new shirt is much bigger compared to the previous shirt.
Its size is fine.
Now, it is comfortable.
Compared to the small shirt, this is better.
I smile and go near the counter.
"This shirt fits well," I tell the shopkeeper.
The shopkeeper smiles and says, "Excellent, madam."
He puts the new shirt in my bag.
"Thank you for the easy exchange, brother," I say.
I take the bag and go out of the shop.
Outside on the street, the humid wind is blowing.
But now I am unworried.
I have a raincoat and a new shirt.
I am fully prepared for the Mumbai monsoon.
I go home happily.
